WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.439
There are so many new beauty products

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.807
being released all the time,

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.509
so we gathered some of the most hyped

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:12.145
from the last month to test for ourselves.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.546
First up, we have the Fenty Beauty

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.849
Bright Fix Eye Brightener Concealer.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.317
I feel like I was confused

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.019
as to what this actually was,

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.954
because the shade range actually had

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.255
normal concealer shades

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.724
and what I would consider
more corrector shades.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.226
So I went with the peach one to use

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:29.562
as a corrector/brightener
under my concealer.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:30.964
I guess it's supposed to conceal

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.632
and brighten and correct.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.567
I did like the brightening
effect with this,

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.102
although it is more subtle.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.138
I feel like it's super
lightweight and blendable.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.906
It's not a thick consistency at all,

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.341
so you can layer it up if you want.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.609
That's what I tried to do.

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:43.710
However, I don't 
think the

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.245
effect is that impressive

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:48.615
where I can say it's worth $25.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.384
I was very intrigued by this KVD Beauty

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.019
ModCon Liquid-Gel Blush,

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:56.089
just because of the term "Liquid-Gel."

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:58.224
The texture of this is very bizarre.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.360
It's very thin, and it feels like nothing.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.195
I can't even explain it well.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.364
But I was nervous to
put this on foundation,

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.766
because I felt like it
was going to break it up.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.935
It didn't. I actually liked this way more

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.336
than I thought I was going to,

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.539
but it is a little sheer for me.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:13.740
I did end up adding more,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.575
but the problem when you do that is that

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:18.478
it adds more shininess,
which I didn't love,

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.913
but I don't hate this.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:24.484
I'm gonna say that $26
for it feels excessive.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.953
NYX came out with this Lip Lingerie XXL

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.054
Matte Liquid Lipstick,

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.556
which reminded me a lot of its

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.724
Shine Loud High Shine Lip Color,

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.126
only without the gloss.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:35.829
NYX, please shorten your product names.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.063
It's basically that,

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.599
but just a more matte liquid lipstick.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.801
I'm a fully converted gloss girl now,

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.369
so applying a liquid lipstick

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.671
did have me stressed out,

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.773
but the formula is actually pretty nice.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.074
I did one thin layer,

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.243
which I think is key
for products like this

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.378
because I find that
they do not layer well,

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:55.115
but one layer was all I
needed for full coverage.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.483
I ate,

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:57.917
I drank,

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.253
and I wore this lipstick
for over eight hours,

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.721
and it stayed looking good.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:02.889
It's pretty transfer-proof.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.358
I did see some fading on
the inside of my mouth,

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.393
but overall I think this is great,

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:10.530
for people who are into
this sort of thing.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.799
I was so excited for this

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.001
Maybelline Fit Me Tinted Moisturizer,

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.836
because I love the Fit Me line

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.105
and skin tints are so popular right now,

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:21.708
but this sucked so bad.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.510
I'm so disappointed.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.512
Off of the face, the texture honestly

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.313
felt really nice and hydrating.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.082
But then I started applying,

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.017
and it dried down so quickly,

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.452
I couldn't blend it in.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:34.487
I was beating my own face with my sponge,

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.623
trying to get it to move, and it didn't.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:39.159
I completely removed it
and reapplied it again,

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:42.662
but it still was not the
most flattering on my skin.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.464
I just think it made my texture worse

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.366
and also caked up in some areas

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.768
and overall just looked very not good.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.770
Don't buy this one.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.005
Next, we have the Givenchy

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.674
Prisme Libre Loose Powder.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.209
I feel like I said that in Spanish,

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.777
but it's supposed to be French.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.312
I'm going to start off by saying

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.147
I really liked this,

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:02.715
but that is not me saying

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:05.084
you need a $58 setting powder.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:07.320
I'm just saying if you were looking

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.289
for a $58 setting powder,

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:10.557
I would get this one.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:13.193
The multicolored powder thing looks cool,

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:14.360
but they all kind of blend into

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.262
one pretty translucent shade.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.964
I think this actually did a nice job

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.299
of smoothing out my pores,

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:21.935
and it set my makeup
without making me feel dry.

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:23.169
I did feel like there was

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.505
some illuminating effect,
which is what I think

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.740
the green and purple powders are for.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.778
But this has a very perfumy
smell, which I hate.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.613
I choked several times.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:36.382
Let's ban scents in
makeup. Thank you so much.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.552
And, lastly, we have another weird blush.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.956
This is the Bite Beauty
Daycation Whipped Cream Blush.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.624
I feel like the worst part

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.859
about this blush is the packaging.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.028
It's so hard to get any product out,

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.197
and when you do, it
just kind of shoots out,

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:54.100
so you get so much product
and kind of waste it.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.469
But I do like the texture.
It's kind of mousse-y,

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:59.038
and the color of the blush
itself is very pretty.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.808
It's glowy, but I feel like
it's a little too metallic

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.943
for it to look like natural dewiness,

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.678
if that makes any sense.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.547
I do feel like the metallicness

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:08.915
enhanced my texture a bit,

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.016
but it wasn't too bad.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.918
I just think that for $32,

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.420
I've tried better liquid-blush formulas.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.155
But you can actually use this on the eyes,

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.358
and I like it more as
kind of a cream shadow

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:19.626
than I do as a blush.

